EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# Sentry crash reporting (optional — app works without it)
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://your-sentry-dsn@sentry.io/project-id

# Google Sign-In + Calendar API (Phase 3)
# Calendar scope ONLY — Gmail scopes were removed so the app can publish to
# Production without Google's restricted-scope (CASA) verification. Email
# features open Gmail compose URLs / mailto instead of the Gmail API.
# Web flow goes through Supabase OAuth; setup at https://console.cloud.google.com:
#   1. Create a project, enable the Google Calendar API
#   2. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External; add the calendar scope;
#      add test-user emails while in Testing mode)
#   3. Create an OAuth client ID of type "Web application":
#      - Authorized JavaScript origins: https://waypointchild.com
#      - Authorized redirect URI: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#      → EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID (also acts as the feature flag on web)
#   4. Supabase dashboard → Authentication → Sign In/Providers → Google:
#      enable, paste the web client ID + secret. Also enable "manual linking"
#      in Auth settings (Profile's Connect Google uses linkIdentity).
#   5. Edge function secrets (for server-side token refresh):
#      supabase secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=... GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#   6. (Native later) OAuth client ID of type "iOS" with bundle id
#      com.waypoint.app → EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID
# Google Sign-In stays hidden in the app until these are set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Epic FHIR / MyChart (roadmap 6.3 — register at https://fhir.epic.com, see ROADMAP.md)
EXPO_PUBLIC_FHIR_CLIENT_ID=your-epic-client-id

# To set up:
# 1. Create a Supabase project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Copy your Project URL and anon key from Settings → API
# 3. Enable pgvector extension in Database → Extensions
# 4. (Optional) Create a Sentry project at https://sentry.io for crash reporting
# 5. Copy this file to .env and fill in your values
